  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Aggressive/Violent Nature Claims",
  "description": "This stereotype falsely claims that Black people are inherently aggressive or violent, often using metaphors related to music or rhythm (e.g., 'love a good beat') to imply that their cultural expression is linked to physicality or aggression. This is a harmful and offensive racial trope used to dehumanize and justify discrimination.",
